From fda3fe557f611ce589bc359e03c4dc2009c99b1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:14:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 372/372] DOS-PORT: patch 0372 -- lever L2: a GUI whose only change is
 some controls marks their rects, not the GUI (DOSAGS_GUI_CTRL_MARK, default
 off)

Why: in Maniac Mansion Deluxe every walk click flips a property of the action-line label (GUI 0's only control, 320x10)
and the next tick flips it back. R3 (0368) then re-marks the whole 320x56 GUI twice per click: the room is restored
under it, GUI 0 and the overlapping verb bar (GUI 1) are re-composited, and the present pushes 44,800 px. At DOSBox-X
fixed 40000 a flip tick costs scene 10.2 + render 5.3 ms against ~1.0 + 0.6 for an ordinary room-1 tick; on the 486
these ticks run ~50 ms (dosags docs/lab/LAB-RB.md section 3.1, LAB-L2G.md).

What: DOSAGS_GUI_CTRL_MARK unset or 0 = off (the 0371 head; the default); exactly "1" = on; any other value = off.
Each GUI counts what flagged it since its last texture redraw (Common/gui/guimain.cpp, Engine/gui/gui_engine.cpp):
GUIObject::MarkChanged() records the control; GUIMain::MarkControlChanged() calls are counted; NotifyControlPosition
and a NotifyControlState with a change make the GUI ineligible. When dos_port_gui_flush_unmarked() finds an unmarked
GUI flagged only that way -- every control mark matched, no GUI-level change, the same position / size / transparency /
z, an idempotent composite (0234), not a 32-bit alpha GUI, at most 16 controls -- it marks, ahead of the restore, for
each such control and every label with text macros, the union of the graphic rect it had at the GUI's last texture
redraw and the one it has now (frame + CalcGraphicRect clipped and unclipped), and the GUI takes R3's unchanged path
(no mark at the composite, drawn once per dirty box that reaches it). Outside the marked rects the redrawn texture
equals the one on screen, so R3's argument holds as for an unchanged GUI. Any failed condition takes the 0371 path; a
flag set between the flush and the texture redraw drops it and R3's late mark of the whole rect follows. A label's rect
is cached on everything CalcGraphicRect reads (text as drawn, translation, font, alignment, size, padding, border and
wrap flags, a font generation bumped by MarkForFontUpdate); labels with macros always recompute. Per-GUI slots are
allocated on first use. The driver, R2 (0369/0370), the restore and the present are unchanged. All of it is under
__DJGPP__.
Witness: "DOS-PORT guictrlmark DOSAGS_GUI_CTRL_MARK=<v|(default)> mode=<0|1>", read at every flush and printed once at
the first scene; "DOS-PORT guictrlmark_final mode= l2= ctrls= px= px_gui= no_safe= unsafe= mixed= props= norec=
slots_overflow= late= mismatch= calc= cache_hits=" in RUNMANI.LOG in both flavours. DOSAGS_GUI_CTRL_MARK joins the
RUNMANIFEST env allowlist. Lab lever: dosags docs/lab/LAB-L2G.md section 8 (lab-l2g2.diff), landed unchanged but for
the comments and the __DJGPP__ guard around its three includes in draw.cpp.

Gates (DOSBox-X fixed 40000, every tick rendered, frame digest + PRESENT_VERIFY, seeded, R2 at its 0370 default in
both arms; dosags tests/harness/results/L2LAND-2026-11-09): off vs on EQUAL on every loop counter of MMD fixtures G
(3164), V (3964), GCL (7004), H (7004), the intro (1299) and AGS Quest AutoPilot (3558), each cell also EQUAL to
LAB-L2G's, each off arm EQUAL to 0371's; a lab check comparing the old GUI texture with the redrawn one found 0
differing pixels outside the marked rects in every on cell (L2 engaged 18 / 19 / 34 / 16 / 10 / 43 times). Controls:
marking nothing DIFF (6049/7004), the rects 1 px short DIFF (2921). Forced, on vs off EQUAL: a control moved /
resized (falls back), GUI visibility / transparency toggled, a label's text grown and shrunk, the slot cap forced to 2
(slots_overflow 4). With DOSAGS_ROUTE_PREWARM=1 in both arms (0371 + 0372 together) EQUAL. Release, on vs off: 5 Days
room 3, Trilby room 35, AGS Quest game output EQUAL; P9-shape MMD with it unset EQUAL to the 0371 release. +8289 bytes
in both flavours (instrumented: .text +5632, .bss +1536; release: .text +5120, .data +512, .bss +1536; both flavours
byte-identical across two clean builds).

